// Fayette County, Ohio — curated directory of meaningful links.
// Single source of truth for the app. Keep entries verified and current.
// Fields: name, category, subcategory, url, description
// Last reviewed: 2026-11-09
//
// Every URL below was fetched and its content checked against the organization
// it claims to be. Sites that block automated fetching (the Board of Elections,
// the Carnegie Public Library, the Record-Herald and the United Way) were checked
// in a browser.
//
// THINGS THAT CHANGED SINCE JULY
//
//   * Southern State Community College's Fayette Campus closed in 2022; Kettering
//     Health turned the building into its Fayette County Health Center.
//   * The Auditor switched to ISSG software (fayettecountyauditor.org); the
//     Treasurer has its own ISSG site.
//   * Hospice of Fayette County is now Ohio's Hospice Washington Court House.
//   * The Record-Herald was sold to HD Media in 2026; its print edition is part of
//     The Connector with the Wilmington and Hillsboro papers. The website is current.
//   * The old ODNR Deer Creek park link redirects; the current ohiodnr.gov page is
//     used.
//
// TRAPS
//
//   Fayette County PA/KY (Lexington)/GA/IN/IL/TN/WV/TX/IA/AL; the VILLAGE of
//   Fayette is in Fulton County. Jeffersonville IN (jefflibrary.org,
//   jeffparks.org); Bloomingburg NY.
//
// GEOGRAPHY
//
//   * One city (Washington Court House, the seat), villages Jeffersonville,
//     Bloomingburg, New Holland (partly Pickaway), Milledgeville and Octa (no
//     sites), and ten townships (Jefferson and Union have pages).
//   * Two county-based school districts (WCH City, Miami Trace). The ESC (Southern
//     Ohio ESC) and career campus (Great Oaks Laurel Oaks) are in Wilmington;
//     mental health is the Paint Valley ADAMH Board (Chillicothe).
//   * Deer Creek State Park straddles Fayette and Pickaway; its main facilities
//     are on the Pickaway side.
//   * Fayette Madison Transit is run by the Community Action Commission.
//
// LEFT OUT
//
//   * 9-1-1 center, RPHF solid waste district, regional planning, port
//     authority/CIC: no websites found.
//   * Historical Society museum, Habitat, community foundation, food pantries,
//     Destination Outlets: no own sites (Facebook or directories only).
//   * Main Street Fayette: site shows only 2024 events.

